  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 579eb66038bb3954284ad438592184d6, type: 3}
  m_Name: DialogueLine_question2-sisterElaboration
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _speaker: You
  _scene: 0
  _recollection: {fileID: 0}
  _lines:
  - It's not entirely her fault, although sometimes it feels like it is.
  - "She's adopted. And, of course, she's still my sister and that shouldn't change
    anything about our relationship\u2014 I love her unconditionally."
  - 'But it does mean that although my family has tried our best, her developmental
    years were spent in an unsafe environment that has quite literally given her
    brain damage. '
  - 'And the trauma certainly doesn''t help. '
  - It doesn't happen as much now, but she used to lash out dangerously. Spending
    hours scream-crying and throwing things and hitting things and nothing you did
    could help her.
  - 'It was scary. '
  - 'It still is. '
  - Having different scream matches everyday multiple times a day in all parts of
    the house certainly didn't do anything good for my mental health.
  - Again, she's much better now. But it doesn't undo that damage.
